 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Marco painted his house black, so his cat moved in next door.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.122
  },
  {
   "text": "Next door stood Nina's plain white house. So why are houses in sunny towns white?",
   "s": 3.322,
   "e": 7.321
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Black is back!\" Marco shouted. Tourists took 400 selfies with his house.",
   "s": 7.621,
   "e": 11.487
  },
  {
   "text": "Nina's house got zero. Marco called it \"a giant sugar cube.\"",
   "s": 11.687,
   "e": 14.872
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the heat wave hit. Day one: his doorknob needed oven mitts.",
   "s": 14.992,
   "e": 18.331
  },
  {
   "text": "Day two: his front step fried an egg. Nobody asked it to.",
   "s": 18.531,
   "e": 21.433
  },
  {
   "text": "Day three: his sprinkler hit the wall, and the whole house steamed like a teapot.",
   "s": 21.633,
   "e": 24.359
  },
  {
   "text": "Meanwhile, Mango the cat napped on Nina's roof, cool as a cucumber.",
   "s": 24.559,
   "e": 27.94
  },
  {
   "text": "So what did the sugar cube know?",
   "s": 28.14,
   "e": 29.338
  },
  {
   "text": "White bounces sunshine away. Black soaks it up, like a black T-shirt at the beach.",
   "s": 29.638,
   "e": 33.662
  },
  {
   "text": "That heat goes straight inside. Marco's living room hit 40 degrees.",
   "s": 33.862,
   "e": 37.568
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Black is back,\" Marco whispered, from Nina's kiddie pool.",
   "s": 37.968,
   "e": 40.447
  },
  {
   "text": "On Saturday, he painted it white. And Mango is back.",
   "s": 40.647,
   "e": 43.432
  }
 ],
